{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/947274-promethean-setting-idea-cofd-revealed-meets-robot-renegades","id":947274,"title":"Promethean Setting Idea: CofD Revealed Meets Robot Renegades","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-09T15:42:28-07:00","id":947274,"title":"Promethean Setting Idea: CofD Revealed Meets Robot Renegades","content":"So, some of my favorite sources of inspiration for Promethean are other narratives about created life, most commonly robots. This gave me the idea for a possible future setting/Chronicle seed for Promethean: in the nearish future, the supernatural has been revealed (in whatever form it exists in, possibly meaning that only Pyros-related phenomena exist), and the governments of the world struggled to handled and regulate it, especially due to the danger posed by Prometheans. <br /> <br /> The discovery of the Pilgrimage by the wider world seemed like it would help assauge fears of the Created, but it had unintended consequences. The government, eager to seem accepting and compassionate while also assuring humans that they were being protected, established a strict set of laws requiring all Prometheans to submit to intense regulation and monitoring, to essentially force them to dedicate themselves entirely to the Pilgrimage. Now, the Centimani exist as an underground resistance movement fighting for Promethean rights, and those Prometheans who want the freedom to live as themselves must hide and flee from the forces of the BPAP- the Bureau for the Protection of Alchemical Persons, a privatized military organization that hunts down Prometheans to force them into assimilation. <br /> <br /> Alchemy was revealed as well, but it's practitioners face their own challenges. Corporate interests and religious lobbying have led to alchemy becoming strictly regulated. Capitalist forces are terrified of its potential to create a post-scarcity society: the pharmaceutical injury doesn't want a panacea, because if there's a pill that makes you never sick again, they're out of a job. Social darwinism guised as naturalism has become an increasingly powerful force in society, and its proponents fear that alchemical enhancement could &quot;upset the natural order&quot; by giving the &quot;unfit&quot; greater ability. Those alchemists not willing to be work under corporate overlords have been forced underground as well. <br /> <br /> From a gameplay perspective, players would take on the roles of Promethean or alchemist fugitives, the Prometheans fighting for their own existence and the alchemists fighting to break down the oppressive structures that keep their work from actually helping society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T15:50:33-07:00","id":947281,"title":"","content":"I like this idea. I was just thinking of combining Demons CyberPunk city Shard with Deviant. I think this would slot into that really well too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T15:57:50-07:00","id":947288,"title":"","content":"I was going to say, Deviants could fit in as well. <br /> <br /> As for aesthetics, the things that most influenced the idea were Asimov's robot stories, The Protomen and Janelle Monae, so I'm imagining the future world as having a sort of retro, art-deco dieselpunk vibe. <br /> <br /> It'd be much more scifi than horror, since it's a deliberate pastiche of &quot;robot underclass&quot; science fiction stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T15:58:49-07:00","id":947289,"title":"","content":"&quot;retro, art-deco dieselpunk&quot; may as well be my middle name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T16:06:43-07:00","id":947294,"title":"","content":"I'm probably gonna include it as a setting seed in an appendix to The Lightning Chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T21:38:51-07:00","id":949104,"title":"","content":"You know, this concept actually gave me an idea for how to handle the Centimani in The Lightning Chronicle. I'm considering not making them a Refinement, but instead the closest thing Prometheans have to a community, a scattered underground support network.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}